  "answer": "A technical support answer must qualify the public help center claim by noting that precise page- and paragraph-level PDF citations are **highly dependent on document quality** [NL-002#NL-002-S09]. For image-only and low-quality scans, the PDF lacks a native text layer, so KnowledgeHub must run OCR [NL-002#NL-002-S09] [NL-006#NL-006-S03]. Because OCR is a heuristic process, blurry, low-resolution, misaligned, handwritten, or complex-layout scans can produce misread characters or broken text blocks, which may cause missing citations, incorrect page links, or TutorChat stating it cannot find the answer [NL-002#NL-002-S09] [NL-006#NL-006-S03] [NL-028#NL-028-S03]. The support answer should therefore add that image-only and low-quality scanned PDFs may not support reliable citations, and customers should be advised to upload native text-based or text-searchable digital files instead [NL-002#NL-002-S09] [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
